		{
			"id":"405ca8fed23dd617",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### 2. The Freshly Carved Star-Eyes → _The Empty Star Watches_\n\n[[Visage]] Triggers\n\n**Trigger:** A PC stares into the newly etched eyes for too long.\n\n**Vision:**  \nThe constellations blink. The stars dissolve. In their place yawns a hole in the sky — a starless void ringed with nothingness. The player feels their body unraveling at its edges, not burning or tearing, but _ceasing_. In that void, they sense not malice, but inevitability, as if a tide has turned toward them. Then, in the depths, a flicker: violet light. Not from the void, but from somewhere _within themselves_.\n\n**Message Implied:** The Wanderer does not hate — it simply unmakes. Eldhoof’s power is the first crack.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The Dome Above → _The Cage Ceiling_\n\n[[Visage]] triggers\n\n**Trigger:** A PC addresses the dome or throws something upward.\n\n**Vision:**  \nThe dome is gone. The player is falling upward into endless black, surrounded not by stars but by gaps where stars should be. Each void flickers like an open wound, and through them, something vast and eyeless stirs. The player realizes — it is not above them, but beneath everything. The dome is not a ceiling. It is a _lid_. And it is beginning to lift.\n\n**Message Implied:** The Wanderer’s prison is weakening, not just here, but everywhere.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Frozen Windows → _The Veins of Elsewhere_\n\n[[Tyris]] triggers\n\n**Trigger:** A PC presses a hand or weapon against the ice.\n\n**Vision:**  \nThe world outside is gone. Through the ice they see a desert where shadows stretch impossibly long, an ocean boiling under a black sun, a city of titans half-swallowed in stone. In each landscape, the same violet cracks vein through the air like fractures in glass. One vision lingers — a lone figure in tattered regalia, his face hidden, standing before an army of corpses. His crown burns with violet fire. The ice pulses once, then the vision fades.\n\n**Message Implied:** Eldhoof is not building a kingdom — he is fraying the seals, across worlds.\n\n---\n\n### 5. The Floor Spiral → _The Weak Point_\n\n**Trigger:** A PC stands at the spiral’s center for more than a moment.\n\n**Vision:**  \nThe spiral beneath their feet glows faintly violet. The chamber melts away, replaced by a dizzying view of the cosmos — not stars, but threads, each strand of existence stretching outward into infinity. One by one, those threads fray and unravel, dissolving into the dark. The player feels their own lifeline tug, as if ready to snap. Then a sudden pressure clamps it still — something vast is holding it, not to save them, but to _study them_. The vision ends.\n\n**Message Implied:** The Wanderer is aware of them now.\n\n---\n\n### 6. The Silence Itself → _The Giants’ Last Gambit_\n\n**Trigger:** A PC fails a Wisdom save or focuses intently on the silence.\n\n**Vision:**  \nThe silence becomes a roar. The player is surrounded by giants frozen mid-battle, their mouths open in unheard screams. Their city crumbles around them, not with fire or quake, but with _absence_ — towers vanish into nothingness, walls fade into blank stone. Above, the Empty Star burns, not with light but with the hunger of a collapsed sun. The hum they hear is not silence — it is the void chanting one word, in every tongue: _Witness._\n\n**Message Implied:** The giants’ “Great Silence” was not victory — it was desperation.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2200,
			"y":-380,
			"width":1200,
			"height":1580
