		{
			"id":"1257232fc5b21c5f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Session Start\n\nYou step across the threshold, leaving behind the spiralling immensity of the Frozen Library. The shift is immediate, almost physical. The weight of a million silent stories falls away, and for a moment you breathe easier — until you realize this silence is different. Not watchful. Not oppressive. Reverent.\n\nThe five pedestals stand empty. Their burden is gone, yet they linger, quiet monuments to a history that has already slipped from the world’s memory — the forgotten truths of [[Old Jotenheim]].\n\nThe chamber itself is a perfect circle, some eighty feet across, yet it feels vaster than any hall you’ve walked. Its ceiling vaults upward into a dome of black stone, seamless and so impossibly high that your eyes cannot find its end. The walls are the same polished, obsidian-like material as the library, surfaces that seem to swallow light and return only a deep, soul-draining cold.\n\nEtched upon those walls is a spiralling mural — a map of the heavens. Not a navigator’s guide, but a chronicle of something older, greater, more terrifying. At first, the stars seem a random scatter, but soon patterns emerge. Constellations twist into vast, unblinking eyes that gaze inward toward the chamber. Following the spiral upward, you see the etchings weaken, fade, blur with age. Yet here — at your own height — the sequence breaks. A handful of eyes are carved with shocking clarity, fresh as if etched only days ago. They gleam when the filtered light touches them, and in that light, it feels as though they shift… watching _you_.\n\nThe illumination comes from five narrow windows set deep in the stone. Each is sealed by a flawless sheet of magical ice, the mountain’s own glacier pressing in from beyond. The harsh glare of the world outside has been softened, fractured, transformed into a milky radiance that casts no warmth — a funeral glow.\n\nThe silence is almost unbearable. Cold air presses against your lungs, heavy with stillness. Your footsteps crunch faintly on frost, but otherwise there is nothing — not even the distant groan of ice. The chamber itself feels as though it is holding its breath. Waiting.\n\nAnd then you notice it: the faintest vibration in your chest, a pulse that isn’t your own heartbeat. The stone seems alive, as though the chamber itself is listening for your next words.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1000,
			"y":-1479,
			"width":860,
			"height":805
		},
		{
			"id":"923fbb37ba60ba88",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Phase 2: Witness to the Clash\n\nThere, two titans clash.\n\nOne is a mountain of white-blue flesh wrapped in broken scales of ice-forged steel. His braided beard is matted with blood and rime, his colossal axe blackened from countless blows. His form staggers, but his eyes burn with grim duty. This is **Ornn**, last of his patrol, standing against fate itself.\n\nThe other is his mirror made monstrous. **Vigmar**, once a frost giant lord in his own right, is now a twisted colossus of flesh, stone, and corruption. Violet veins seethe across his body like cracks in broken glass, spilling light with each labored movement. His weapon — a shattered obelisk wielded as a club — drips with spectral fire. Where Ornn bleeds, Vigmar burns. Where Ornn breathes, Vigmar whispers. His voice carries the same alien hum you heard in the sanctum: _Witness. Witness. Witness._\n\nThe ground is a battlefield of broken pillars and gouged earth, a graveyard of half-buried giant forms — some still statues of ice and stone, others twisted, corrupted, shattered.\n\nAnd you arrive at the **apex of their war**.\n\n## Phase 2: Witness to the Clash\n\n**Scene:** Players stand at the battlefield’s edge as Ornn and Vigmar fight.\n\n- **Environment:** The glacier shakes. Crystal spires crack and topple. Buried giant corpses twitch under corruption.\n- **Skill Prompt:** Insight or Arcana (DC 15) reveals Vigmar’s voice is layered — his words are being _fed_ through the Wanderer’s hum.\n\n**Hazards / Interactions:**\n\n1. **Falling Crystal Spires** — Players must move or risk being pinned. Dex Save (DC 14). If pinned, Str/Athletics (DC 16) or an ally’s help to break free.\n2. **Vigmar’s Corruption Surges** — Violet tendrils lash out. Players can:\n    - Attack them (AC 15, 15hp tendril).\n    - Endure (Con Save DC 15, take 2d8 necrotic on fail).\n    - Counterspell/Dispel to weaken.\n\n_Effect:_ Success helps Ornn land his next blow with strength. Failure leaves Ornn visibly weakened, adding gravitas to his determination.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3640,
			"y":-1806,
			"width":760,
			"height":1043
		},
		{
			"id":"5c033729201ae1b2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## The Apex of War\n\nWith a roar that splits the sky, Ornn drives his axe deep into Vigmar’s chest. The sound is a mountain breaking. Violet fire erupts in a geyser, bathing the glacier in sickly light. Vigmar staggers, collapsing to one knee. For a heartbeat, his true voice slips through the corruption, rumbling in sorrow:\n\n**Vigmar:**\n\n> “Brother… the silence was too heavy. I thought him release… but he was only the end. Forgive me.”\n\nOrnn leans close, pressing one hand against his brother’s chest, his voice a trembling roar of grief:\n\n**Ornn:**\n\n> “You were my shield in the long vigil. My voice in the silence. And now… you are my doom. I forgive nothing—  \n> and I forgive everything.”\n\nWith a final heave, Ornn wrenches his axe free. Vigmar collapses in ruin, still at last.\n\n## Phase 3: The Apex of War\n\n**Beat 1: The Killing Strike**\n\n- Ornn drives his axe deep into Vigmar’s chest. Violet fire erupts. The plateau shakes.\n\n**Beat 2: Vigmar’s Last Words**\n- Vigmar whispers, voice fractured: _“I thought him release… but he was only the end. Forgive me.”_\n- If a PC succeeds on Religion or Persuasion (DC 16), Vigmar’s true voice cuts through for a moment, letting Ornn hear his brother untainted.   \n\n**Beat 3: Ornn’s Response**\n\n- Ornn’s line: _“You were my shield in the silence… my doom… I forgive nothing, and I forgive everything.”_\n- If players shout encouragement, Ornn includes them in his words: _“…and now, you are witness.”_",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":4560,
			"y":-1731,
			"width":900,
			"height":893
		},
		{
			"id":"38de89290deb71c8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## The Seal Shatters\n\nBut death is no victory. The violet veins crawl from Vigmar’s corpse into Ornn’s wounds, hungrily seizing their last anchor. His body spasms, the corruption racing to claim him as it did his brother.\n\nWith a roar of pure defiance, Ornn slams his mailed fist into a crystal spire. The bone shatters with a sickening crack, but the agony drives the corruption back for a moment. His breath comes ragged, his voice raw with desperation as his eyes turn to you.\n\n**Ornn (to the party):**\n\n> “Hear me. We were the last guardians of Old Jotenheim — the final seal upon the Empty Star. My life, my brother’s life, bound to its prison. And now… now the cage is broken.”\n\nBlood spatters the snow as he coughs, violet fire spilling faintly from the wound.\n\n**Ornn:**\n\n> “The Wanderer wakes… and Vaalameer drinks its strength. You must carry this warning. Swear it! Swear it, or all is unmade.”\n\nHe thrusts a runed stone into your hands — its surface cold as the void, heavy as grief.\n\n## Phase 4: The Seal Shatters\n\n**Beat 1: Vigmar Collapses**\n- Vigmar falls, his corrupted corpse spasming with violet light. His body cracks the glacier.\n\n**Beat 2: The Pulse of the Wanderer**\n- A shockwave erupts, unavoidable. Each player makes a choice on _how they endure_:\n    - **Con Save (DC 15):** Resist physically — you are battered but steady.\n    - **Wis Save (DC 15):** Endure mentally — glimpse a vision of the Wanderer.\n    - **Cha Save (DC 15):** Assert your will — the hum whispers to you personally.\n\n_Success:_ Gain a fragment of forbidden knowledge (describe as cosmic vision).  \n_Failure:_ Take 2 levels of exhaustion OR gain a corruption mark (nightmares, faint violet veins, whispers).",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":5730,
			"y":-1774,
			"width":900,
			"height":980
		},
		{
			"id":"e5004e59332bf6a2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Constitution (The Body / The Corpse)\n\nThese visions reveal the _physical_ cost of the Wanderer’s presence — how it manifests in flesh, matter, and undeath.\n\n- **Core Realization:** The undead are not “rebellions against life.” They are _pockets of entropy,_ hollowed shells that weaken reality from within.\n- **Detail Layers:**\n    - You glimpse a battlefield where fallen soldiers do not rot but remain perfectly preserved, their veins glowing violet. They are not bodies anymore — they are _anchors_, cracks through which the Wanderer’s absence spreads.\n    - Necromancy is not just “magic that manipulates life” — it is the application of the Wanderer’s principle of _un-making_. Each skeleton raised is another thread snipped from reality’s weave.\n    - The more undead exist, the weaker the prison becomes. The armies of the Lich King aren’t just soldiers — they are _chisels,_ battering the walls of the Wanderer’s cage.\n\n**Player Takeaway:** The fight against undeath is not moral. It is existential. Every necromancer, lich, and zombie is feeding the Wanderer’s escape.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":5170,
			"y":-3087,
			"width":620,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"a6e1b42bc9d6fb1e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Wisdom (The Mind / The Pattern)\n\nThese visions reveal the _cosmic truth_ of the Wanderer — its nature as inevitability rather than intent.\n\n- **Core Realization:** The Wanderer is not evil. It is not conscious in the way mortals understand. It is inevitability given form — entropy made witness.\n- **Detail Layers:**\n    \n    - You glimpse threads of existence woven across the void, glowing strands that stretch from plane to plane. One by one, they fray and dissolve, not cut, not torn — simply _cease_.\n    - You see the gods — architects of reality — hammering the first stones of creation. Behind them, always, the Wanderer waits. It was not defeated. It was _written around._\n    - The “Empty Star” is not truly a star. It is the scar left in the heavens where the Wanderer’s prison was knotted into place. Its movement is not orbit, but unraveling.\n\n**Player Takeaway:** The Wanderer cannot be “killed” or “banished.” It can only be delayed, resisted, contained. Those who seek to “use” it (like Vaalameer) are mistaking the tide for a sword.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":5830,
			"y":-3087,
			"width":700,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"3c73e0a159eab502",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Charisma (The Will / The Bond)\n\nThese visions reveal the _personal danger_ of the Wanderer — how its influence seeps through desire, identity, and power.\n\n- **Core Realization:** The Wanderer does not seduce with promises of glory. It erodes by offering release — from silence, from futility, from mortality.\n- **Detail Layers:**\n    - You glimpse King Ymir in New Jotenheim, his chest cracked open to reveal the Rime-Heart. Around him, his people stand silent, their wills frozen. You realize: they are not simply slaves to Vaalameer. They are _conduits,_ the plague turning their very loyalty into fuel for the Wanderer.\n    - You glimpse Vaalameer himself, his crown of violet fire burning brighter than his flesh. He does not serve the Wanderer knowingly — he believes he _masters_ it. But in truth, he is its greatest tool. His ambition creates the cracks through which entropy seeps.\n    - Finally, you glimpse yourself — or a shadow of yourself — standing in silence beside the Empty Star. Your lips do not move, but you hear your own voice whisper: _“I would be free of burden. I would be still.”_\n\n**Player Takeaway:** Anyone — even they — could become a vessel of the Wanderer, not through corruption of body but through surrender of will.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":6570,
			"y":-3087,
			"width":780,
			"height":580
		},
		{"id":"88f8cb14d8908027","type":"file","file":"NPCs/Jotenheim/Ornn.md","x":5040,"y":-567,"width":500,"height":800},
		{"id":"f318632235d039cb","type":"file","file":"NPCs/Jotenheim/Vigmar.md","x":4460,"y":-567,"width":520,"height":800},
		{
			"id":"e98ba191630de697",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Players Actions.\n\nThe sessions starts; \n\nThe PC's find the treasure trove. \n\n[[Visage]] and [[Tyris]] encountered visions being in the dome.\n\nPC's left the dome, the dome collapsed.\n\nInstead of going towards the fighting, the PC's decided to find shelter to long rest. \n\nThe PC's encountered a minor combat with spiders. The spiders died. Easily. After dealing psychic damage to Visage and Tyris.\n\nThe PC's attempted a long rest where the corrupted vines and spiders attacked.\n\nOn the second watch, spiders and vines tried to get into the room where the pc's where staying.\n\nPC's then where chased out of the city where the city turned into a void. Each were given a small vision. \n\nEnd of session.\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-80,
			"y":-2731,
			"width":920,
			"height":840
		},
		{
			"id":"d82c32c5dcc5c1d5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Visions of the Wanderer’s Pulse\n\n## Constitution Save (Body Endurance)\n\n_You resist the physical annihilation — your body fights to hold itself together against the unraveling force. But survival comes at the cost of clarity._\n\n- **Success:** You glimpse your own body in a mirror of ice, but it’s wrong. Limbs dissolve into frost, your outline bleeds into the void. You see yourself as the Wanderer sees you: _a temporary stain upon silence._ When you blink, it’s gone — but for a heartbeat, you’re unsure if you are still whole.\n- **Failure:** Pain sears through your veins as violet light pulses under your skin like cracks in glass. They fade in moments, but leave faint ghost-lines only you notice. Whispers follow: _“This flesh is borrowed. It can be unmade.”_\n\n## Wisdom Save (Mind Endurance)\n\n_You brace your thoughts against the pulse, but your awareness stretches thin — too thin — across realities._\n\n- **Success:** You stand beneath a sky without stars. Not black, but _absent_, a vast canvas of nothing. At its center burns a hollow sun, not radiating light but consuming it. You understand, instinctively, that this is the **Empty Star**. It does not hate. It does not hunger. It simply _undoes_. You return gasping, knowledge lodged like a thorn in your mind.\n- **Failure:** You hear a voice — not loud, not whispered, but inevitable. It speaks in your own thoughts, without sound:  \n    _“You saw me. You know me. You are mine.”_  \n    For the briefest instant, you believe it — and the belief terrifies you more than the words.\n\n## Charisma Save (Will Endurance)\n\n_You assert yourself against the Wanderer’s pulse, but the price is contact. You push — and it pushes back._\n\n- **Success:** You find yourself standing on an endless frozen plain. In the distance, a figure approaches: tall, armored, its crown burning violet flame. You realize with a start — it is the **Lich King Vaalameer**, but his form is bloated, distorted, like a shadow cast too wide. He raises a hand, palm open, as though offering alliance — but behind him, a vast, starless void yawns. You snap back before your will breaks.\n    \n- **Failure:** A shadow of yourself steps from your body, formed of violet light and darkness. It smiles — your smile, but wrong. It leans close and whispers: _“You will serve. You already have.”_ The vision fades, but the echo of its voice lingers in your head.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1080,
			"y":-1634,
			"width":900,
			"height":960
		},
		{"id":"40cd6ef51063a5e7","type":"file","file":"NPCs/Gods/The Wanderer Corruption Table.md","x":2120,"y":-2074,"width":1220,"height":1840},
		{
			"id":"e9f8b1b1898462d3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Phase 6: The Aftermath\n\n- **Environmental Consequence:** The sky darkens. A star vanishes. The hum becomes an omnipresent background noise. The world itself acknowledges the Wanderer’s release.\n- **Party Consequence:** They carry the Message Stone, the oath (or broken oath), and the trauma of witnessing the last guardians fall.\n- **Narrative Consequence:** Ornn’s death is exactly as the players choose. They cannot stop the seal’s breaking — but they _decide how it is remembered_.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2120,
			"y":-2411,
			"width":1220,
			"height":201
		},
		{
			"id":"626437e6914eca00",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## The Pulse of the Wanderer\n\nBefore you can answer, the plateau convulses. A shockwave rips outward from Vigmar’s corpse, a pulse that passes _through_ you, not around you.\n\nYour lungs seize. Your vision whites out. For an instant, your very flesh seems to unravel at its edges. Your thoughts echo back on themselves, stretched thin until only silence remains.\n\nAnd then you see it: not with eyes, but with your soul.\n\nA starless void. A hole in the heavens where no light belongs. A presence that is not presence at all. The Wanderer. The Empty Star. Watching. Waiting. _Released._\n\nThe vision collapses. You find yourselves hurled forward, snow stinging your faces, boots crunching onto the battlefield itself. Behind you, the sanctum is gone — shattered windows spilling frost and silence into the void.\n\nBefore you, Ornn staggers, violet veins crawling up his body. He falls to one knee, axe slipping from his grasp. His eyes burn with one last plea.\n\n**Ornn:**\n\n> “Mercy… give me mercy. Better nothing… than his thrall.”\n\nThe world holds its breath for your answer\n\n## Phase 5: Ornn’s Last Stand\n\n**Beat 1: Corruption Crawls**\n\n- Violet veins surge into Ornn. He smashes his fist against a crystal spire, bone shattering, holding it back for moments longer.\n\n**Beat 2: The Plea**  \nOrnn turns to the party, voice ragged:\n\n> “We were the seal. My life, my brother’s life — the last chains on the Empty Star. Now the cage is broken. Swear it! Swear you will carry this warning, or all is unmade!”\n\nHe thrusts forward the **Message Stone**. Whoever takes it becomes its bearer.\n\n**Beat 3: The Mercy Choice**\n\n- Ornn begs: _“Strike me down. Better nothing than his thrall.”_\n- Players can:\n    1. **Grant mercy:** Deliver the killing blow. Ornn dies clean, dignified.\n    2. **Hesitate:** Ornn drives his own axe into his chest, defiant but tragic.\n    3. **Refuse:** The corruption briefly surges — his body twitches, almost rising as a thrall — before Ornn smashes himself against the ice to deny it.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1080,
			"y":-2891,
			"width":900,
			"height":1160
		},
		{
			"id":"0f3e81120a518b7f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Optional “Twist” for Agency\n\nEach failed save can leave a **small corruption scar** (not mechanical unless you want, but narratively potent):\n\n- **Con:** faint violet veins visible under skin when stressed.\n- **Wis:** recurring nightmares of the Empty Star.\n- **Cha:** occasionally hear your own voice speaking when you haven’t spoken.\n\nEach success can grant a **fragment of forbidden knowledge**:\n\n- **Con:** awareness of how undead “hollow” flesh for the Wanderer.\n- **Wis:** realization that the Wanderer doesn’t act with malice, but inevitability.\n- **Cha:** a fleeting recognition of Vaalameer’s tie to the Wanderer.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":5730,
			"y":-2300,
			"width":900,
			"height":420
		}
	],
